/ 06) LENNY ELEKMAN

/     LEONARD w ELEKMAN IS A MEMBER OF THE WCFMPG AND CLOSE COLLEAGUE OF RICHARD
/     LARY.  TOGETHER, THEY CREATED THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM AND SEVERAL NOTABLE
/     IMPLEMENTATIONS OF THE BASIC LANGUAGE INCLUDING POLY BASIC [LATER SOLD BY
/     DEC AS EDU-SYSTEM 30].

/     LENNY SINGLE HANDEDLY WROTE 4K BASIC, A STANDALONE IMPLEMENTATION THAT
/     USES EVERY MEMORY LOCATION IN A 4K PDP-8 EXCEPT THOSE USED BY THE RIM
/     LOADER.  WHILE IT IS NOT POSSIBLE TO INTERFACE THE PROGRAM TO A
/     STORAGE-BASED OPERATING SYSTEM [UNLESS IMPLEMENTED VIRTUALLY], 4K BASIC IS
/     THE BASIS FOR 8K BASIC, A VARIANT CREATED BY JACK BURNESS.  AS NORMALLY
/     DISTRIBUTED, THIS PROGRAM CAN BE LOADED AND STARTED FROM THE R-L MONITOR
/     AND P?S/8 BUT NOT OS/8, WHICH IS DESTROYED IN MEMORY IN THE INITIALIZATION
/     PHASE OF THE PROGRAM.  [NOTE: OS/8 MUST BE COMPLETELY DISABLED AT PROGRAM
/     STARTUP; SUFFICIENT OS/8 CODE IS STILL PRESENT IN MEMORY TO DAMAGE THE
/     OS/8 SYSTEM DEVICE IF THE MACHINE IS RESTARTED AT 07600; FULL MANUAL
/     BOOTSTRAP IS REQUIRED TO SAFELY RESTART THE MACHINE.]

/     A LONG-TERM P?S/8 PROJECT IS TO INTERFACE 8K BASIC TO P?S/8 INCLUDING FILE
/     SUPPORT.  AT LEAST 8K WILL BE REQUIRED WITH 12K RECOMMENDED FOR MAXIMUM
/     PERFORMANCE.  BASIC PROGRAMS OCCUPYING UP TO EIGHT TFS FILES WILL BE
/     SUPPORTED. [NOTE: BASIC FILES CANNOT BE EDITED OUTSIDE OF BASIC; THE
/     KEYBOARD MONITOR WILL BE CAPABLE OF FILE MAINTENANCE ONLY; TFS TEXT FILES
/     REQUIRE LINE NUMBERS IMPLEMENTED WITHIN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR AND
/     INTEGRATED EDITOR.  BASIC FILES CONTAIN LINES WHERE THE LINE NUMBER IS
/     PART OF THE FILE CONTEXT; THE DIGITS OF THE LINE NUMBERS ARE TEXT
/     CHARACTERS.  ADDITIONALLY, BASIC FILES CONTAIN INTEGRITY CHECK INFORMATION
/     PARTICULAR TO THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION.]
/ 07) EMPER0R

/     THIS IS AN HONORIFIC BESTOWED UPON MARIO DENOBILI [BY HIMSELF].  SOME OF
/     HIS PSYCOPHANTS ARE KNOWN TO HAVE CONTRARIAN VIEWS REGARDING THE USE OF
