/     MANUAL OPERATIONS ASSOCIATED WITH TOGGLING IN THE ENTIRE R-L MONITOR.  BY
/     BEING EXPOSED TO CO-ROUTINES, HIS ENTIRE APPROACH TO PROGRAMMING HAS BEEN
/     CHANGED FOREVER; IN MANY WAYS HIS LIFE HAS BEEN TOTALLY RUINED FROM THAT
/     MOMENT ONWARD [WHICH IS PROBABLY A GOOD THING IN THE END].

/     HE IS ALSO RESPONSIBLE FOR THIS ENTIRE DOCUMENT, EVERY LAST CHARACTER FROM
/     THE BEGINNING TO THE END.  [YOU MAY PERIODICALLY PONDER THIS AS YOU PORE
/     THROUGH IT FOR A TIME.]
/ 11) LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY

/     THE P?S/8 LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS AN OPTIONAL COMPONENT OF P?S/8 THAT
/     PROVIDES ALTERNATE CONSOLE AND LINEPRINTER SERVICES TO ALL COMPLIANT
/     PROGRAMS THROUGHOUT P?S/8 [INCLUDING USER-WRITTEN PROGRAMS].  EXTENDED
/     MEMORY IS REQUIRED TO ENABLE THE OVERLAY; AS A RESULT, THE LOGICAL MEMORY
/     SIZE MUST BE REDUCED BY ONE ENTIRE MEMORY FIELD [UNLESS ALREADY REDUCED BY
/     ANOTHER SYSTEM COMPONENT SUCH AS AN EXTENDED SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER].

/     COMPLIANT PROGRAMS REPLACE THEIR INTERNAL CODE FOR THE DEVICE 03/04
/     CONSOLE TERMINAL AND/OR DEVICE 66 LINEPRINTER WITH LOGICAL CALLS TO
/     SPECIFIC LOCATIONS ON PAGE ZERO OF THE HIGHEST FIELD OF MEMORY.  THE P?S/8
/     MEMORY STATUS WORD PROVIDES ALL RELEVANT INFORMATION.  CALLS ARE PROVIDED
/     FOR CONSOLE INPUT, CONSOLE OUTPUT, LINEPRINTER OUTPUT AND LINEPRINTER
/     INPUT [USED ONLY FOR ACTIVE PARTICIPATION IN POTENTIAL FLOW-CONTROL
/     MECHANISMS].  A LOGICAL INTERRUPT HANDLER IS PROVIDED TO BE HOOKED INTO
/     ANY INTERRUPT-DRIVEN PROGRAM [AHEAD OF ANY PHYSICAL CONSOLE DEVICE
/     HANDLING].  THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION OF FOCAL, 1969 USES THIS MECHANISM
/     FOR ALL RELEVANT INTERRUPT HANDLING.

/     WHEN THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED, ALL SYSTEM DEVICE ERRORS ARE
/     REDIRECTED TO THE OVERLAY; THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER NO LONGER HALTS FOR
/     ERROR RECOVERY PURPOSES; INSTEAD, AN ERROR-HANDLING PORTION OF THE OVERLAY
/     IS USED TO ALERT THE USER TO ANY ERRORS WITH SEVERAL OPTIONS [RETRY, EXIT,
/     ETC.].  DEPENDING ON THE CONFIGURATION, VERBOSE ERROR MESSAGES CAN BE USED
/     SPECIFIC TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE HARDWARE.  FOR EXAMPLE, WHEN USED WITH THE
/     TC01/TC08 HANDLER, IT IS POSSIBLE TO GET EXPLICIT NOTICE OF SELECT,
/     TIMING, MARK, PARITY AND END ERRORS.

/     CERTAIN SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS DEFINE ENHANCEMENTS TO BE CARRIED OUT BY
/     THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY.  FOR EXAMPLE, THE TC01/TC08 HANDLER USES A
/     COMMON VALUE FOR THE LAST BLOCK TRANSFERRED; THIS IS USED TO DETERMINE THE
/     BEST INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION BASED ON LAST KNOWN BLOCK TRANSFER.
/     HOWEVER, IF THE SYSTEM DEVICE UNIT IS CHANGED, THIS CAN CAUSE AN
/     OCCASIONAL WRONG GUESS [INSTANTLY CORRECTED ONCE REALIZED TO BE IN ERROR].
/     THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY WILL ENHANCE THE DEVICE HANDLER TO USE A TABLE
/     OF LAST TRANSFERRED BLOCKS, ONE FOR EACH LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT TOTALLY
/     PREVENTING THIS MINOR PROBLEM.

/     THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY CAN BE CONFIGURED TO SUPPORT A VARIETY OF
/     PHYSICAL ALTERNATE CONSOLE DEVICES SUCH AS THE VT8E AS AN EMULATED
/     TERMINAL, OR THE VR12/VR14 DISPLAY ON THE PDP-12.  DEVICES SIMILAR TO THE
/     DEFAULT CONSOLE CAN ALSO BE SUPPORTED SUCH AS A TERMINAL CONNECTED TO A
/     DEVICE 10/11 PT08 OR KL8JA OR OTHER INTERFACE. ALTERNATE PRINTING DEVICES
/     ARE ALSO SUPPORTED SUCH AS THE LS-120 SERIAL PRINTER WHICH REQUIRES
/     REVERSE CHANNEL FLOW CONTROL.

/     SINCE THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY ONLY INTERFACES WITH COMPLIANT PROGRAMS
/     AND THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER, IT IS AVAILABLE FROM THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT
/     AS WELL AS THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM.
/ 12) HANK MAURER

/     HANK IS A MEMBER OF THE WCFMPG AND AUTHOR OF VARIOUS HIGH-LEVEL LANGUAGE
/     IMPLEMENTATIONS OF BASIC AND CERTAIN OTHER ODD LANGUAGES.  SOME OF HIS
/     WORK IS FOUND IN FULL RELEASES OF THE R-L MONITOR AND OTHER PROJECTS
/     WITHIN DEC [SOMETIMES WITHOUT DEC'S KNOWLEDGE] SUCH AS DIBOL-8, THE
/     PRECURSOR OF COS-300/310. [NOTE: THE ORIGINAL DIBOL-8 IS ACTUALLY A SYSTEM
/     PROGRAM ON A HACKED-UP VERSION OF THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM WITH THE COMMAND
/     NAMES PATCHED; THERE IS AN INCESTUOUS RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN P?S/8 AND
/     VARIOUS IMPLEMENTATIONS OF COS.]

/ 13) OS/8

/     OS/8 IS THE MOST WELL KNOWN OF LATER MARKETING NAMES OF THE ORIGINAL PS/8
/     PROJECT STARTED AS A WEEKEND HACK BY RICHARD LARY.  WHILE MANY WILL
/     ATTRIBUTE THIS MEDIOCRE SYSTEM TO RICHIE, IT IS ACTUALLY THE WORK OF MANY
/     PEOPLE [ARGUABLY TOO MANY PEOPLE] AND SUFFERS FROM A VARIETY OF WEAKNESSES
/     TRACEABLE TO POOR DESIGN OR MANAGERIAL INTERFERENCE PREVENTING EVOLVEMENT
/     OF THE INITIAL DESIGN TO SOMETHING BETTER.  IT WAS NEVER PROPERLY VETTED
/     BY THE PDP-8 PROGRAMMING COMMUNITY; MANAGEMENT INTERFERENCE EVENTUALLY
/     PREVENTED CHANGES CAUSING IT TO BECOME ESSENTIALLY FIXATED WITH A LOT OF
/     LIMITATIONS.  FOR EXAMPLE, THE SYSTEM FILE DATE RECKONING REACHED
/     EXPIRATION IN 1978, ALTHOUGH A SERIES OF KLUDGES MANAGED TO KEEP MOST
/     USERS IGNORANT [YET VAGUELY SATISFIED] UNTIL 2001.  BY THAT TIME DEC WAS
/     NO LONGER MARKETING THE PDP-8 OR ITS DESCENDANTS.

/     OS/8 WAS ALSO ALLOWED TO DEVOLVE INTO SEVERAL INCOMPATIBLE VARIANTS AS
/     QUICK-FIX ATTEMPTS TO SOLVE VARIOUS HARDWARE COMPATIBILITY PROBLEMS.
/     WITHOUT MAJOR REDESIGN IT IS QUITE IMPOSSIBLE TO CREATE A UNIFIED SYSTEM
/     THAT CAN HANDLE ALL OF THE NEEDLESS PROBLEMS THAT AROSE.  SOME OF THESE
/     VARIANTS ARE KNOWN AS OS/78, OS/278 ETC. AND ASSOCIATEFD WITH VARIOUS
/     VERSION NUMBERS FOR THE RELEASE.  IN SOME CASES, THESE DISTINCTIONS ARE
/     MARKETING PLOYS WHILE IN OTHERS IT IS THE DIRECT RESULT OF PRAGMATIC
/     ATTEMPTS TO RUN ON SPECIFIC MODELS SUCH AS THE DECMATES.  SOME VARIANTS
/     ARE MORE DYSFUNCTIONAL THAN OTHERS DUE TO A VARIETY OF REASONS, OFTEN
/     ASSOCIATED WITH BOTH MANAGERIAL AND PROGRAMMER INCOMPETENCE.

/     OS/8 COMMANDS AND INTERNAL STRUCTURE ARE BARELY ACCEPTABLE TO USERS
/     SEEKING THE GENERAL SENSIBILITIES OF MOST DEC OPERATING SYSTEMS IF VARIOUS
/     LIMITATIONS ARE ACCEPTED.  TO MANY, THIS IS NOT THE CASE, ESPECIALLY DUE
/     TO SORE POINT PROBLEMS SUCH AS MODERN TERMINAL CONTROL REQUIREMENTS AND
/     PROPER HANDLING OF LARGER DISK STORAGE DEVICES, POOR FILE NAMING AND
/     DATE ISSUES, ETC.  [NOTE: THESE ARE NOT HINDSIGHT ISSUES AS VIRTUALLY ALL
/     OF THESE PROBLEMS WERE DISCUSSED DURING THE PRODUCT'S ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT
/     CYCLE.]
/     THE P?S/8 OPTIONAL SHELL WILL ADD POWERFUL CAPABILITY TO THE BASIC P?S/8
/     SYSTEM, WHICH ALREADY OPERATES IN A MANNER QUITE SIMILAR TO MOST DEC
/     OPERATING SYSTEMS. [NOTE: THERE ARE SOME DIFFERENCES, MOSTLY TRACEABLE TO
/     THE PRIMITIVE TFS FILE SYSTEM.  HOWEVER, OTHER ASPECTS OF P?S/8 ARE
/     ACTUALLY MORE IN LINE WITH TYPICAL SYSTEMS DEVELOPED ON OTHER DEC
/     MACHINES.] AS SUCH, THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE P?S/8 SHELL WILL ESSENTIALLY
/     OBSOLETE OS/8; IT WILL BE DIFFICULT TO FIND EVEN A NITPICK FEATURE OF OS/8
/     THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT DOESN'T PROVIDE A PROPER EQUIVALENT TO [OR MORE
/     LIKELY AN IMPROVEMENT].  IT IS INTENDED TO MIGRATE ALL RELEVANT OS/8-BASED
/     SYSTEM PROGRAMS AND/OR PROVIDE P?S/8 SHELL EQUIVALENT UTILITIES.  DUE TO
/     THE NATURE OF MOST OS/8 SYSTEM PROGRAMS WITH VIRTUALLY IDENTICAL INTERNAL
/     INTERFACE TO THE OPERATING SYSTEM, IT IS EXPECTED TO BE A RELATIVELY
/     STRAIGHTFORWARD MATTER [AT THE SOURCE CODE LEVEL] TO MIGRATE ALL
/     MEANINGFUL PROGRAMS. [NOTE: SOME HAVE NICKNAMED THE P?S/8 SHELL "THE OS/8
/     KILLER".]

/ 14) PS/8

/     PS/8 IS THE ORIGINAL MARKETING NAME GIVEN TO A QUICK AND DIRTY OPERATING
/     SYSTEM HACKED UP OVER A WEEKEND BY RICHARD LARY.

/     THE ORIGINAL NAME OF THIS WORK WAS THE FIRST UPWARD COMPATIBLE KEYBOARD
/     EDITOR AND MONITOR [NOTE THE OBVIOUS ACRONYM].  [PLANNED BUT NEVER
/     IMPLEMENTED WAS A SECOND UPWARD COMPATIBLE KEYBOARD EDITOR AND MONITOR.]
/     THE INTERNALS OF THIS SYSTEM WERE NEVER FULLY VETTED LEADING TO MANY
/     LIMITATIONS CRITICIZED BY MANY PEOPLE, MOST NOTABLY CHARLES LASNER, CHIEF
/     ARCHITECT OF THE P?S/8 PROJECT. [NOTE: CHARLES WAS RECRUITED TO WORK ON
/     THIS SYSTEM BUT DECLINED IN FAVOR OF IMPROVING THE R-L MONITOR.  HE IS
/     ALSO THE AUTHOR OF KERMIT-12 FOR OS/8 AND HAS HAD THE DUBIOUS DISTINCTION
/     OF WRITING ADDITIONAL UTILITIES FOR OS/8 TO SUPPORT THE KERMIT PROJECT.]

/     BY THE TIME MANAGERIAL DECISION WAS MADE TO MARKET IT [AS PS/8] THE DESIGN
/     BECAME STAGNATED WITH LITTLE ABILITY TO IMPROVE; HALF-FINISHED FEATURES
/     THAT DON'T FUNCTION PROPERLY ABOUND AND WILL REMAIN SO INDEFINITELY.
/     [NOTE: THE MOST NOTABLE LIMITATION IS A SEGMENTED DIRECTORY THAT WOULD
/     SUGGEST THE ABILITY TO ADJUST THE OVERALL DIRECTORY SIZE; HOWEVER, IN NOW
/     STAGNATED IMPLEMENTATION, THERE IS NO PRACTICAL ABILITY TO EITHER LENGTHEN
/     OR SHORTEN THE DIRECTORY.  AS SUCH, THE RESULT IS A WORST CASE OUTCOME; ON
/     SMALL DEVICES THE DIRECTORY IS GENERALLY TOO LONG.  ON LARGER DEVICES, IT
/     IS ALL TOO EASY TO RUN OUT OF DIRECTORY ENTRY SPACE LONG BEFORE THE
/     UNDERLYING STORAGE IS COMPLETELY USED.  THE SEGMENTATION MERELY
/     CONTRIBUTES TO THIS PROBLEM AS A POINTLESS SOURCE OF OVERHEAD THAT
/     REQUIRES ADDITIONAL PROGRAMMING TO ACCESS.]

/     AT THE REQUEST OF A DEC SALESMAN, THE NAME WAS CHANGED TO OS/8 BECAUSE HE
/     FELT IT WAS DIFFICULT TO SELL CUSTOMERS ON A "PROGRAMMING" SYSTEM AS
/     OPPOSED TO AN "OPERATING" SYSTEM.
/ 15) P?S

/     P?S IS THE SHORTHAND DESIGNATION FOR THE POLY QUESTION SOCIETY, AN
/     AMORPHOUS GROUP OF QUESTIONERS ONCE LOCATED AT BROOKLYN POLYTECHNIC
/     INSTITUTE, 333 JAY STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11201.  VARIOUS MEMBERS ARE KNOWN
/     TO HAVE ACHIEVED EXTRAORDINARY FEATS OF COMPUTER PROGRAMMING, OFTEN
/     PIONEERING EFFORTS.  ONE OF ITS MOST FAMOUS MEMBERS IS RICHARD LARY [AKA
/     "RICHIE" OR "MOUTH"], CREATOR OF THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM AND MANY OTHER
/     FAMOUS PDP-8 PROGRAMS AND OTHER EXTRAORDINARY THINGS INCLUDING SEVERAL
/     VALUABLE SOFTWARE PATENTS.

/ 16) P?S/8

/     P?S/8 IS THE NAME OF AN OPERATING SYSTEM FOR THE PDP-8.  IT IS BASED, IN
/     PART, ON THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM.  ALL OF THE DEVELOPERS OF P?S/8 ARE
/     EXPERIENCED PROGRAMMERS WHO STARTED THEIR PDP-8 PROGRAMMING CAREERS ON THE
/     R-L MONITOR SYSTEM AND ARE THOROUGHLY FAMILIAR WITH IT INTERNALLY AS WELL
/     AS EXPERT USERS OF THAT PIONEERING SYSTEM.  BY KNOWING ITS WEAKNESSES AND
/     OVERCOMING THEM IN NEW PROGRAMMING, A BETTER OVERALL SYSTEM WAS CREATED.

/     THE REGULAR USER INTERFACE TO P?S/8 IS BASED ON USER EXPERIENCE WITH
/     ORIGINAL IMPLEMENTATIONS OF THE BASIC LANGUAGE AS PRACTICED ON VARIOUS
/     GE-235 TIME-SHARING SYSTEMS.  FILE COMMANDS ARE VERY MINIMAL AND GEARED
/     TOWARDS BEING AS INOBSTRUSIVE AS POSSIBLE.  MOST USERS INTUITIVELY
/     UNDERSTAND THIS INTERFACE WITHIN MOMENTS OF FIRST CONTACT WITH P?S/8.

/     WHILE MAINTAINING THE ORIGINAL STYLE AND SUBSTANCE OF THE R-L MONITOR, THE
/     OUTGROWTH OF P?S/8 IS TOTALLY ALONG THE LINES OF OTHER OPERATING SYSTEMS
/     FROM DEC FOR OTHER COMPUTERS.  HOWEVER, UNLIKE OS/8, THE EMPHASIS HAS BEEN
/     ON EFFICIENCY OF RESOURCES AND SPEED OF PERFORMANCE, ESPECIALLY ON SLOWER
/     DEVICES SUCH AS DECTAPES AND LINCTAPES.  MOST USERS, GIVEN AN INFORMED
/     CHOICE, WILL PREFER P?S/8 TO OS/8 FOR A VARIETY OF REASONS.

/     P?S/8 HAS CERTAIN LIMITATIONS, NOT SO MUCH AS TO IMPLEMENTATION, BUT
/     TO THE DELIBERATE ATTEMPT TO MAXIMIZE PERFORMANCE WHILE PROVIDING ADEQUATE
/     PRODUCTIVITY FEATURES; THIS IS NOT TO EVERYONE'S LIKING.  FOR THOSE WHO
/     PREFER A LARGER FEATURE SET, P?S/8 IS BEING EXPANDED TO INCLUDE AN
/     OPTIONAL SHELL OVERLAY.   THIS WILL OPERATE UNDER AN ENTIRELY DIFFERENT
/     SET OF TRADE-OFFS GENERALLY REQUIRING MORE MEMORY.

/     FOR MOST USERS, THE OPTIONAL SHELL WILL NOT BE NEEDED.  HOWEVER, "POWER
/     USERS" WILL PREFER THE P?S/8 SHELL OVER THE BASIC SYSTEM [AS WELL AS OS/8]
/     FOR GENERAL USE WITHOUT RESTRICTIONS.  WHILE THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT WILL
/     REQUIRE MORE RESOURCES THAN THE BASIC ENVIRONMENT, PERFORMANCE WILL STILL
/     EXCEED THAT OF OS/8; ALL ATTEMPTS WILL BE MADE TO OBTAIN MAXIMUM
/     PERFORMANCE FROM THE RESOURCES AVAILABLE.  HOWEVER, THE BASIC SYSTEM IS
/     4K-ORIENTED. [FOR REFERENCE, OS/8 IS 8K-ORIENTED.] THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT
/     IS ORIENTED TOWARDS LARGER CONFIGURATIONS; CERTAIN FEATURES WILL WORK BEST
/     IN AS MUCH AS 24K OR MORE; A FEW WILL REQUIRE 32K TO WORK AS BEST AS
/     POSSIBLE; A SMALL FEW FEATURES WILL NOT BE AVAILABLE IN A 4K ENVIRONMENT,
/     GENERALLY LEADING TO GRACEFUL ERROR MESSAGES.
/     BY ADJUSTING CERTAIN CONFIGURATION PARAMETERS, THE SCOPE OF FUNCTIONALITY
/     CAN BE ROUGHLY THE SAME AS AN EQUIVALENT OS/8 SYSTEM GIVEN THE IDENTICAL
/     HARDWARE.  HOWEVER, PERFORMANCE WILL BE BETTER IN THE P?S/8 SHELL IN MANY
/     WAYS.  SINCE THE CONFIGURATION IS QUITE FLEXIBLE, THE USER CAN DETERMINE
/     WHAT IS BEST FOR THE PRESENT USAGE.  FOR THE MOST SOPHISTICATED USERS,
/     SEVERAL VARIATIONS USED JUDICIOUSLY MAY BE THE BEST OVERALL SOLUTION
/     UNLESS 32K IS AVAILABLE. [NOTE: CERTAIN SYSTEM CONFIGURATION PARAMETERS
/     CAN BE ADJUSTED TO OBTAIN TRADEOFFS WITH DIFFERENT OUTCOMES.]  DUE TO THE
/     VARIOUS FEATURES OF P?S/8 THAT ARE IMPLEMENTED IN A FAR MORE COMPREHENSIVE
/     WAY THAN OS/8, COUPLED WITH OPTIONAL FEATURES THAT HAVE NO OS/8
/     EQUIVALENT, IT MAY BE DIFFICULT TO COMPARE PERFORMANCE OF THE TWO SYSTEMS
/     DIRECTLY. [NOTE: OS/8 DOES NOT SUPPORT ALTERNATE CONSOLE DEVICES OR
/     MODERN TERMINAL FLOW-CONTROL OTHER THAN WHEN USED WITH A SPECIFIC OUTPUT
/     HANDLER [KNOWN AS THE KL8E HANDLER].  UNFORTUNATELY, MOST CONSOLE OUTPUT
/     IS PERFORMED DIRECTLY BY EACH PROGRAM.  THUS, COMPARING THE ERRATIC
/     PERFORMANCE OF OS/8 PROGRAMS TO THE SYSTEM-WIDE APPROACH OF P?S/8 WHERE
/     ALL CONFORMING PROGRAMS ARE FULLY COMPLIANT WITH RESPECT TO BOTH TERMINAL
/     HANDLING AND LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY INTERFACE IS NOT EASILY GAUGED.  MANY
/     USERS WITH TERMINALS SUCH AS THE VT100 FAMILY HAVE COMPROMISED THEIR
/     SYSTEMS TO LIMIT THE AMOUNT OF FLAWED OUTPUT FROM OS/8; P?S/8 CAN RUN
/     AT ANY CONNECTION RATE WITHOUT DROPPING A SINGLE CHARACTER.]

/     NOTE: P?S/8 WAS DEMONSTRATED TO DEC PERSONNEL WITH THE INTENTION OF GIVING
/     THE SOFTWARE TO DEC IN EXCHANGE FOR HARDWARE DONATION TO THE BROOKLYN
/     POLYTECHNIC INSTITUTE, WHERE ALL MEMBERS OF THE WCFMPG AND P?S ONCE MET
/     [NOT NECESSARILY AT THE SAME TIME].  THIS WAS ACTUALLY ATEMPTED TWICE.
/     HOWEVER, DEC MANAGEMENT REJECTED P?S/8 FOR REASONS THAT DEFY RATIONAL
/     EXPLANATION DESPITE ACTIVE PARTICIPATION BY SOME OF THE INDIVIDUALS
/     MENTIONED IN THIS DOCUMENT AS WELL AS OTHER MEMBERS OF THE DEC PDP-8
/     PROGRAMMING STAFF LOBBYING FOR IT.

/     EVENTUALLY, A LIMITED EDITION OF P?S/8 [RENAMED IFDOS] WAS LICENSED TO
/     INTERSIL CORPORATION FOR USE ON THEIR INTERCEPT I, A PDP-8-COMPATIBLE
/     MACHINE BASED ON THE IM6100 AND SIMILAR TO AN INFERIOR OFFERING FROM DEC
/     KNOWN AS THE VT78, THE SLOWEST SYSTEM CONFIGURATION SUPPORTED BY P?S/8.
/     FOR SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER CONSIDERATIONS ALONE, P?S/8 RUNS 13 TIMES AS
/     FAST AS OS/8 ON THIS MACHINE.  SINCE THE INTERCEPT I IS 20 PERCENT FASTER
/     THAN THE VT78, OS/8 PERFORMANCE IS MODESTLY BETTER ON THIS MACHINE.  ON
/     EITHER MACHINE, PERFORMANCE COMPARISONS SHOW A DRAMATIC DIFFERENCE BETWEEN
/     THE TWO OPERATING SYSTEMS.
/     [NOTE: P?S/8 ACTUALLY RUNS AT THE SAME SPEED ON THE RX01/RX02 DISKETTE
/     DRIVES REGARDLESS OF THE SPEED OF THE HOST MACHINE.  HOWEVER, OS/8 RUNS
/     13 TIMES AS SLOW ON THE VT78 DUE TO HANDLER INEFFICIENCY THAT CANNOT BE
/     OVERCOME DUE TO DESIGN LIMITATIONS OF OS/8.  THE P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE
/     HANDLER REQUIRES EXTENDED MEMORY AS DOES OS/8; HOWEVER, P?S/8 EXTENDED
/     DEVICE HANDLER DESIGN ALLOWS MUCH MORE CODE SPACE ALLOWING
/     HIGH-PERFORMANCE HANDLING OF RX01/RX02 DRIVES BY USING MORE SOPHISTICATED
/     METHODS.  EVEN ON A SYSTEM AS SLOW AS THE VT78 THE PERFORMANCE IS
/     VIRTUALLY THE SAME AS ON MUCH FASTER HARDWARE.  OS/8 ONLY ALLOWS ENOUGH
/     CODE SPACE TO IMPLEMENT A SEVERELY COMPROMISED DEVICE HANDLER UNABLE TO
/     KEEP UP WITH THE REQUIRED 2:1 INTERLEAVE.  AS SUCH, THE HIGHEST
/     TRACK/SECTOR CALCULATIONS FAIL TO MAINTAIN TRANSFER SPEED ON ALL MODELS;
/     ON VERY SLOW MACHINES SUCH AS THE VT78, THIS LOSS OF PERFORMANCE APPLIES
/     TO VIRTUALLY EVERY DISKETTE SECTOR.  MOST USERS OF THE RX01/RX02 DISKETTE
/     DRIVE, WHEN CONNECTED TO FASTER MACHINES SUCH AS THE PDP-8/E, ARE UNAWARE
/     OF THIS PROBLEM SINCE ONLY THE HIGHEST SECTORS ARE AFFECTED; MOST
/     OPERATIONS ADDRESS LOWER SECTORS WHERE THE PERFORMANCE LOSS DOESN'T SET
/     IN; ON THE VT78 ALL SECTORS ARE AFFECTED WITH THE POSSIBLE EXCEPTION OF A
/     PORTION OF TRACK 1.  OS/8 USES A MINIMAL SIZE DIVISION ALGORITHM
/     IMPLEMENTED BY THE USE OF REPETITIVE SUBTRACTION; ALL TRACK/SECTOR DATA
/     MUST BE CALCULATED EACH AND EVERY TIME.  P?S/8 RX01/RX02 HANDLERS USE A
/     METHOD DERIVED BY STRIPPING DOWN AN EAE SIMULATOR TO A DIRECT
/     IMPLEMENTATION OF THE REQUIRED DIVISION.  HOWEVER, THIS IS ONLY USED ONCE
/     PER CALL TO ESTABLISH THE INITIAL TRACK/SECTOR DATA.  ALL ADDITIONAL
/     SECTORS ARE INSTANTLY CALCULATED BY A PREDICTOR/CORRECTOR ROUTINE.  THE
/     LATEST TRACK AND SECTOR ARE DERIVED FROM THE PREVIOUS VALUES.  THE AMOUNT
/     OF CODE SPACE TO IMPLEMENT THIS TWO-STAGE METHOD IS FAR BEYOND THE UPPER
/     LIMIT OF OS/8 HANDLER DESIGN.]

/ 17) R-L MONITOR SYSTEM

/     THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM IS THE PRECURSOR TO P?S/8 WRITTEN BY RICHARD LARY
/     AND LENNY ELEKMAN.  THE ENTIRE OPERATING SYSTEM WAS HAND ASSEMBLED AND
/     ENTERED DIRECTLY INTO PDP-8 MEMORY MANUALLY ON THE FRONT PANEL OF AN
/     ORIGINAL PDP-8 COMPUTER LOCATED IN THE BROOKLYN POLYTECHNIC INSTITUTE
/     ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING COMPLEX.  ALL OF THE PROGRAMMERS MENTIONED HERE
/     EXTENSIVELY USED THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM AS IT WAS A MAJOR ADVANCE OVER
/     PREVIOUS SYSTEMS FOR THE SAME HARDWARE.

/     [NOTE: THE MANUAL ENTRY OF SO MANY THOUSANDS OF R-L MONITOR INSTRUCTIONS
/     ON THIS COMPUTER CAUSED PREMATURE FAILURE OF THE FRONT PANEL.  CHARLES
/     LASNER HAD THE DUBIOUS DISTINCTION OF MANUALLY CHANGING EVERY ONE OF THE
/     FRONT PANEL SWITCHES TO RESTORE FUNCTIONALITY.  IT IS NOT ADVISABLE TO
/     MENTION THE SWITCH MANUFACTURER'S NAME ["STACKPOLE"] IN HIS PRESENCE.]

/     THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM ONLY SUPPORTS A SINGLE TU55/TU56 DECTAPE DRIVE AND
/     REQUIRES EXTENSIVE MODIFICATION TO SUPPORT ANY ALTERNATE DEVICE.  MEMBERS
/     OF THE P?S INTENSELY STUDIED THE INTERNAL WORKINGS OF THE R-L MONITOR
/     SYSTEM AND BODILY REPLACED VARIOUS SECTIONS OVER THE COURSE OF MANY YEARS,
/     EVENTUALLY PRODUCING THE P?S/8 REPLACEMENT SYSTEM AS DESCRIBED ELSEWHERE
/     IN THIS DOCUMENT.
/     P?S MEMBERS EVENTUALLY SUBMITTED THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM TO DECUS [DIGITAL
/     EQUIPMENT CORPORATION USERS SOCIETY], COMPLETE WITH THE LAST ADDED
/     COMPONENT: FOCAL, 1969 WITH R-L MONITOR MODIFICATIONS BY CHARLES LASNER.
/     THE SUBMITTED NAME WAS MS/8 TO APPEAR MORE IN LINE WITH THE VARIOUS OTHER
/     DEC OFFERINGS OF THE TIME PERIOD [PS/8, OS/8 ETC.].

/     A FEW FEATURES OF THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM ARE RETAINED IN P?S/8 [WITH ALL
/     NEW SOURCE CODE] INCLUDING FULL COMPATIBILITY WITH TFS BINARY FILES [WHICH
/     ARE A PROPER SUBSET OF P?S/8 TFS BINARY FILES].

/ 18) JIM ROTH

/     THE LATE JIM ROTH WAS RESPONSIBLE FOR MANY PROGRAMMING GEMS THROUGHOUT
/     P?S/8.  HE WROTE THE ORIGINAL RAW IMPLEMENTATION OF THE P?S/8 "PAL"
/     ASSEMBLER.  THIS WORK IS A FAST, CLEAN IMPLEMENTATION OF A REPLACEMENT
/     ASSEMBLER FOR DEC'S PAL III ASSEMBLER, WHICH WAS A VERY OLD AND POORLY
/     CODED PROGRAM ALBEIT WITH A MODICUM OF GOOD DESIGN POINTS; HOWEVER, PAL
/     III IS NOT ADAPTABLE TO ADDING ON ANY ADDITIONAL FEATURES.  JIM'S CODE IS
/     QUITE ELEGANT MAKING IT A RELATIVELY STRAIGHT-FORWARD [BUT LENGTHY] TASK
/     TO ADD ON ALL THE ADDITIONAL FEATURES A FULL-FLEDGED PDP-8 ASSEMBLER
/     REQUIRES.  [NOTE: THE REST OF THE ASSEMBLER WAS WRITTEN BY CHARLES LASNER
/     OVER A COURSE OF YEARS.  ADDED FEATURES INCLUDE DUAL MODE LINC ASSEMBLY
/     OPTIONS, LITERAL PROCESSING, QUIRKY SYNTAX SUPPORT [SUCH AS "JMP."],
/     MISCELLANEOUS ASSEMBLER DIRECTIVES AND CROSS-REFERENCE DUMP.]

/     JIM WAS ALSO FASCINATED WITH RICHARD LARY'S "SLURP" LOADER AND WAS ABLE TO
/     CREATE A WORKING VERSION FOR THE DF32 MINIDISK AS PART OF A COMPLETE
/     ALTERNATIVE VERSION OF THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM FOR THE DF32.

/     ALONG THE WAY HE INTENSELY STUDIED THE OPERATION OF THE TC01 CONTROLLER
/     AND IS THE AUTHOR OF MOST OF THE SOMEWHAT CONFUSING SEARCH AND MODE-CHANGE
/     CODE WITHIN THE TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER, INCLUDING THE INITIAL
/     SEARCH GUESS ROUTINE.  AS A DIRECT RESULT OF HIS SIGNIFICANTLY LOWERING
/     THE OVERALL CODE SPACE USED BY THE HANDLER, ENOUGH NEW SPACE WAS OBTAINED
/     TO ENVISION THE IMBEDDED SYSTEM LOADER THAT IS ARGUABLY THE SINGLE MOST
/     IMPORTANT CONTRIBUTION OF P?S/8 OVER THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM AT THE KERNEL
/     LEVEL.

/     WHILE AN EMPLOYEE AT DEC, JIM WROTE THE QUICKSORT ROUTINES FOR
/     REORGANIZING THE SYMBOL TABLE FOR PRINTOUT WITHIN PAL8.  HE IS ALSO
/     RESPONSIBLE FOR EXTENSIVE REWRITE OF CERTAIN SPECIALIZED VERSIONS OF OS/8
/     [INDUSTRIAL] BASIC.  JIM ALSO REMOVED AN ENTIRE PAGE OF CODE SPACE WITHIN
/     POLY SPACEWAR BY USING A MORE ADVANCED TABLE LOOKUP METHOD FOR CALCULATING
/     VARIOUS TRIGONOMETRIC FUNCTIONS.  AS A RESULT, MANY MORE SPECIAL EFFECTS
/     AND OTHER FRILLS BECAME POSSIBLE WHILE STILL RUNNING AS A LEGITIMATE USER
/     PROGRAM COMPATIBLE WITH MOST 4K ENVIRONMENTS.

/     JIM WAS THE ONLY MEMBER OF THE P?S WITH AN ACCOMPLISHED BACKGROUND IN
/     ELECTRONICS BESIDES CHARLES LASNER.  HE ALSO WORKED FOR DEC'S VLSI
/     HARDWARE DIVISION FOR SOME TIME AS WELL AS VARIOUS PDP-8 PROGRAMMING
/     GROUPS.
/ 19) SLURP LOADER

/     RICHARD LARY IMPLEMENTED THE FIRST "SLURP" LOADER [THE TERM ATTEMPTS TO
/     DESCRIBE SOME ASPECTS OF THE PROCESS] AS THE ONLY BINARY FILE LOADER ON
/     THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM.  ALL P?S/8 SYSTEMS PROVIDE A VIRTUAL LOADER THAT
/     PRODUCES SUBSTANTIALLY THE SAME RESULT; WHERE FEASIBLE, THE SLURP LOADER
/     IS PROVIDED AS AN OPTION.  MOST, BUT NOT ALL SUPPORTED DEVICES CAN
/     IMPLEMENT A SLURP LOADER.  EXCEPTIONS INCLUDE THREE-CYCLE DATA BREAK
/     DEVICES THAT ARE TOO FAST [RF08] AND OTHER DMA DEVICES THAT CANNOT BE
/     ACCESSED VIA SINGLE WORD TRANSFERS [RK08/RK01, RK8E/RK05, ETC.].  ALL
/     ASYNCHRONOUS PROGRAM TRANSFER DEVICES SHOULD SUPPORT A SLURP LOADER.

/     SLURP LOADING IS BASED ON AN EFFICIENT LOADING FORMAT THAT IS NEARLY 6/7
/     AS EFFICIENT AS CORE-IMAGE FORMAT [AND FAR MORE EFFICIENT THAN ANY
/     PAPER-TAPE LOADING FORMAT].  THE FORMAT CONSISTS OF A 12-BIT CONTROL WORD
/     CONTAINING SIX TWO-BIT CONTROL FIELDS FOLLOWED BY SIX 12-BIT DATA WORDS.
/     EACH DATA WORD IS EITHER A) A LOADING ADDRESS FOR SUBSEQUENT LOADING, B) A
/     WORD TO BE LOADED INTO THE LATEST ADDRESS; IMPLICITLY INCREMENT THE
/     LOADING ADDRESS, C) A FIELD SETTING [FIELD 0 IS THE DEFAULT], D) END OF
/     FILE.  THE SEVEN-WORD SEQUENCE IS REPEATED 18 TIMES IN ANY SINGLE BLOCK;
/     THE LAST TWO WORDS OF EACH 128-WORD BLOCK ARE IGNORED.

/     OTHER THAN THE PREVAILING LOADING ORIGIN AND CURRENT DATA FIELD SETTING,
/     ALL DATA BLOCKS ARE INDEPENDENT. [NOTE: SLURP FORMAT FILES CAN
/     THEORETICALLY BE CREATED PROVISIONALLY THAT ARE SIGNIFICANTLY LONGER THAN
/     TFS FILES.]

/     A PRACTICAL SLURP LOADER WORKS WITHOUT A BLOCK-ORIENTED BUFFER, PROCESSING
/     THE WORDS AS THEY ARE READ IN DIRECTLY.  IN THE CASE OF THE TC01/TC08
/     DECTAPE, THE WORD-COUNT REGISTER IS SET TO 0000; THE CURRENT ADDRESS IS
/     SET TO ONE LESS THAN THE ADDRESS OF A ONE-WORD BUFFER; JIM ROTH PROVED
/     THAT THE CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER IS A PERFECTLY ACCEPTABLE BUFFER.  THE
/     PROGRAM WAITS FOR THE WORD-COUNT REGISTER TO CHANGE FROM 0000 -> 0001.  AT
/     THAT POINT, THE LATEST FILE WORD IS IN THE CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER.  EACH
/     WORD IS PROCESSED AS DESCRIBED ABOVE.

/     WHEN ALL FILES HAVE BEEN LOADED, THE LOADED PROGRAM IS STARTED AT AN
/     ADDRESS DETERMINED BY THE P?S/8 BIN PROGRAM THAT PLACES THE SLURP LOADER,
/     IN CONJUNCTION WITH USER-SUPPLIED OPTION SWITCHES.  ALL SLURP LOADERS
/     INCLUDE AN INTERNAL ADDRESS OF A HLT INSTRUCTION [7402] TO BE USED AS THE
/     DEFAULT ADDRESS IF THE USER DOESN'T SUPPLY ONE; STARTING ADDRESS AND
/     INITIAL STARTING FIELD ARE PROCESSED AT THE END OF FILE LOADING.

/     A MAJOR ADVANTAGE OF THE SLURP LOADER IS THAT THE DEVICE CAN BE
/     WRITE-PROTECTED AS ALL LOADING IS READ-ONLY.  [NOTE: IF THE VIRTUAL LOADER
/     IS CHOSEN, THE SYSTEM DEVICE MUST BE WRITE-ENABLED AS THE VIRTUAL AREA IS
/     USED TO PROTECT LOADING OVER THE VIRTUAL LOADER INCLUDING ITS BUFFER USED
/     TO READ IN PORTIONS OF BINARY FILES ETC.] THERE IS A NOTICABLE PERFORMANCE
/     IMPROVEMENT BETWEEN THE TWO LOADER VARIANTS; USE OF THE SLURP LOADER IS
/     ALWAYS RECOMMENDED FOR NORMAL USAGE [IF AVAILABLE].

/     THE SLURP LOADER IS INCLUDED IN THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM, POLY BASIC
/     [EDU-SYSTEM 30] AS WELL AS P?S/8.  [NOTE: ONLY THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION
/     SUPPORTS EXTENDED MEMORY.]
/ 20) SYSTEM SAVE AREA

/     THE SYSTEM SAVE AREA REFERS TO THE DEDICATED BLOCKS ON THE P?S/8 SYSTEM
/     DEVICE [BLOCKS 0020-0057] USED TO PRESERVE THE ENTIRE USER AREA CONTENTS
/     OF FIELD 0 [0000-7577].  THIS IS ACCESSED BY VARIOUS MEMORY-ORIENTED
/     COMPONENTS OF BOTH THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM AND THE OPTIONAL SHELL
/     ENVIRONMENT.

/     IN THE BASIC SYSTEM, THE SYSTEM SAVE AREA CAN ALSO BE ADDRESSED BY TWO TFS
/     FILE NAMES "%" AND "$"; EACH TFS FILE IS 2K LONG.  "%" STORES LOCATIONS
/     00000-03777]; "$" STORES LOCATIONS 04000-07777]. [NOTE: THE LAST PAGE OF
/     MEMORY WHERE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER IS RESIDENT IS NEVER OVERWRITTEN;
/     HOWEVER, CERTAIN PROGRAMS MAY WRITE OUT AN IMAGE OF THE DEVICE HANDLER IN
/     CONJUNCTION WITH SAVING THE REST OF FIELD 0.]

/ 21) P?S/8 SHELL

/     THE P?S/8 SHELL IS AN OPTIONAL SYSTEM OVERLAY THAT DISPLACES THE NORMAL
/     KEYBOARD MONITOR IN FAVOR OF AN ALTERNATE INTERFACE AND FILE SYSTEM.  THE
/     SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER IS USED ONLY AS AN INTERNAL MECHANISM TO BIND ALL OF
/     THE SHELL COMPONENTS TOGETHER.  THIS INCLUDES THE SYSTEM LOADER WHICH,
/     UNLIKE THE OS/8 ANALOGOUS SEGMENT, IS SELF-SUFFICIENT AND CANNOT FAIL DUE
/     TO INTERNAL ERROR [UNRECOVERABLE HALT].  IT IS INTENDED TO BE USED WITH
/     THE OPTIONAL LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY; AS SUCH, ALL ERRORS ON THE SYSTEM
/     DEVICE WILL BE ELEGANTLY HANDLED BY THE OPERATING SYSTEM; PROGRAMS DO NOT
/     PARTICIPATE IN THE ERROR RECOVERY PROCESS FOR ANY OPERATION ON THE SYSTEM
/     DEVICE. [NOTE: THE P?S/8 SHELL CANNOT DIRECTLY ACCESS THE TFS DIRECTORY ON
/     THE SYSTEM DEVICE; SPECIFIC UTILITIES CAN BE WRITTEN TO ACCOMPLISH THIS.
/     THIS WILL FACILITATE FILE CONVERSION BETWEEN THE TWO P?S/8 OPERATIONAL
/     VARIANTS AND/OR OS/8.]

/     NO OTHER BASIC P?S/8 FEATURE IS USED IN THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT.  AS SUCH,
/     IT IS FEASIBLE TO STRIP OUT MOST OF THE BASIC SYSTEM TO MINIMIZE THE
/     OVERALL SYSTEM REQUIREMENT IF DESIRED.  BY SUITABLE CONFIGURATION, THE
/     FIRST [UP TO] 4096 BLOCKS CAN BE RESERVED FOR THE SYSTEM DEVICE, WHICH
/     CORRESPONDS TO THE LARGEST POSSIBLE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE STORAGE.  IF
/     BOTH SYSTEM VARIANTS ARE TO BE PRESENT ON ANY DEVICE, THE RESERVED SIZE
/     CAN BE ADJUSTED ACCORDINGLY.  HOWEVER, THE MINIMUM VIABLE SIZE FOR A
/     SYSTEM DEVICE GEARED TOWARDS ROUTINELY RUNNING THE SHELL ON A DAILY BASIS
/     CAN BE SET TO APPROXIMATELY 200 BLOCKS; THIS IS COMPARABLE TO THE
/     DIFFERENCE BETWEEN AN OS/8 SYSTEM DEVICE AND AN OS/8 NON-SYSTEM DEVICE ON
/     THE SAME MEDIA.  AS NECESSARY, ANY ADDITIONAL STORAGE CAN BE ACCESSED AS A
/     NON-SYSTEM DEVICE; P?S/8 INCLUDES A TABLE OF NON-SYSTEM HANDLERS THAT
/     SPECIFIES PROTECTION OFFSETS TO DEAL WITH MIXED CONFIGURATIONS. [NOTE: THE
/     BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM IS ORIENTED TOWARDS THE SMALLER MAXIMUM STORAGE SPACE
/     ADDRESSED BY THE SYSTEM HANDLER.  NON-SYSTEM DEVICES CAN ADDRESS AS MUCH
/     AS 4096 TIMES AS MUCH SPACE.  ALL NON-SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER CALLS ARE THUS
/     POTENTIALLY SUBJECT TO AN ADJUSTMENT ON DEVICES WITH DUAL STRUCTURES
/     PRESENT.]  [NOTE: THE NOTION OF MIXED CONFIGURATIONS IS STILL BEING
/     RESEARCHED AS OF THIS WRITING; ACTUAL IMPLEMENTATION MAY VARY GREATLY.]
/     THE SHELL PROCESSES COMMANDS THAT REFERENCE A FILE SYSTEM FAR MORE
/     POWERFUL THAN THE OS/8 STRUCTURE.  FILE NAMES ARE UP TO 12 CHARACTERS WITH
/     UP TO FOUR CHARACTER FILE EXTENSIONS WITH CASE-RETENTION. [OS/8 FILE NAMES
/     ARE UP TO SIX CHARACTERS WITH UP TO TWO CHARACTER FILE EXTENSIONS IN
/     UPPER-CASE ONLY.]  SINCE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER IS DESIGNED FOR EITHER
/     THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM OR SHELL INTER-COMPONENT COMMUNICATION, IT PLAYS NO
/     DIRECT ROLE IN THE SHELL FILE ACCESS.  POWERFUL NON-SYSTEM HANDLERS ARE
/     USED FOR ALL OPERATIONS WHICH CAN ACCESS FAR MORE STORAGE THAN EITHER THE
/     BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM OR OS/8.

/     THE FOLLOWING IS A REALISTIC COMPARISON: THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM CAN
/     ADDRESS .5 MWORDS OF DATA PER LOGICAL UNIT.  [NOTE: 1.0 MWORDS IS 1048576
/     12-BIT WORDS OF STORAGE.]  ASSUMING EIGHT LOGICAL UNITS PER SYSTEM DEVICE,
/     THIS IS A TOTAL ADDRESSABLE SPACE OF 4.0 MWORDS PER SYSTEM DEVICE GROUP.
/     OS/8 HANDLERS CAN ADDRESS AT MOST 1.0 MWORDS OF STORAGE PER HANDLER.
/     THUS, OS/8 CAN ADDRESS WITH ANY ONE HANDLER TWICE AS MUCH STORAGE SPACE AS
/     ANY ONE P?S/8 LOGICAL DEVICE UNIT WHILE THE ENTIRE P?S/8 DEVICE GROUP CAN
/     ACCESS FOUR TIMES AS MUCH STORAGE AS OS/8'S SYSTEM HANDLER.

/     THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT USES NON-SYSTEM HANDLERS THAT ARE RADICALLY
/     DIFFERENT FROM EITHER THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM OR OS/8.  THE MAXIMUM
/     ADDRESSABLE SPACE IS 2048 MWORDS PER LOGICAL UNIT FOR A TOTAL ADDRESSABLE
/     STORAGE OF 16384 MWORDS PER NON-SYSTEM DEVICE GROUP.  THIS IS 2048 TIMES
/     AS LARGE AS ANY OS/8 HANDLER CAN ACCESS AND 4096 TIMES AS LARGE AS ANY
/     P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER PER LOGICAL UNIT.

/     A FURTHER CONSIDERATION OF STORAGE SPACE IS THE ALLOWED NUMBER OF LOGICAL
/     DEVICES.  OS/8 ALLOWS AT MOST 15 LOGICAL DEVICES.  [NOTE: INTERNAL DEVICE
/     INFORMATION IS HELD IN 4-BIT FIELDS; THE CASE OF 0000 IS NEEDED TO
/     INDICATE A LACK OF EXPLICIT DEVICE TO ALLOW INTERPRETATION AT ANOTHER
/     LEVEL.] AS A PRACTICAL MATTER [FOR COMPARISON PURPOSES] THE NUMBER EIGHT
/     WILL BE USED. [NOTE: ONE OF THE DEVICES IS DSK:, A LOGICAL STAND-IN FOR
/     ONE OF THE OTHER DEVICES; SEVERAL ADDITIONAL DEVICES ARE USED FOR
/     NON-STORAGE PURPOSES SUCH AS THE CONSOLE DEVICE, HIGH-SPEED READER/PUNCH
/     IF APPLICABLE AND SYSTEM LINEPRINTER.] WHILE THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF
/     DEVICES AVAILABLE TO THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT HAS NOT BEEN DETERMINED, THE
/     MAXIMUM NUMBER IS NOT LIMITED TO A SUBSET OF 16; BETTER OVERALL DESIGN
/     ALLOWS FOR FAR MORE DEVICE HANDLER ENTRIES IN A PRACTICAL SYSTEM.  FOR
/     COMPARISON PURPOSES THE NUMBER 32 WILL BE USED [IT COULD EASILY BE TWICE
/     AS MUCH].

/     MORE MODERN STORAGE DEVICES TEND TO BE LARGER HARD DISKS PARTITIONED INTO
/     SMALLER DIVISIONS AS NECESSARY.  THIS SUGGESTS THE LARGEST ADDRESSABLE
/     SPACE ON A SUITABLY PARTITIONED DISK WOULD BE 512 MWORDS.  MANY MORE
/     RECENT DEVICES USE SIX-BIT BYTES IN THE UNDERLYING STORAGE. [NOTE:
/     EXAMPLES INCLUDE RX-SERIES DISKETTES AS TYPICALLY OPERATED IN 12-BIT MODE,
/     RD50 HARD DISK SUBSYSTEM ON CERTAIN DECMATES, CESI MDC8 ETC.  ALL SHARE
/     THE COMMON TRAIT OF USING 3/4 OF THE ACTUAL STORAGE OF 8-BIT BYTES.] THUS,
/     ANOTHER WAY TO STATE CAPACITY IS 4 GB PER LOGICAL DEVICE UNIT, 32 GB PER
/     LOGICAL DEVICE GROUP AND 1.0 TB PER SYSTEM WITHIN THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT.
/     OS/8 ONLY SUPPORTS 2.0 MB MAXIMUM ON ANY DEVICE AND 32 MB ON THE LARGEST
/     SUPPORTABLE SYSTEM.
/     THERE IS AN ADDITIONAL IMPORTANT TRADEOFF: OS/8 RECORD SIZE IS 256 WORDS
/     WHILE ALL P?S/8 HANDLERS ADDRESS STORAGE IN 128 WORD BLOCKS.  DEPENDING ON
/     PROGRAM LOGISTICS, OS/8'S LARGER MINIMUM BUFFER REQUIREMENT CAN CAUSE
/     PROGRAM SIZE TO BE NEEDLESSLY LARGE AND UNWIELDY.  OFTEN A SMALL CONTROL
/     FILE IS NEEDED AND THE SMALLEST FILE BUFFER WOULD BE APPROPRIATE.  IN ANY
/     P?S/8 SITUATION THIS WOULD BE A ONE PAGE BUFFER WHILE OS/8 WOULD DEMAND A
/     TWO PAGE BUFFER; THE OVERALL REQUIREMENT QUICKLY BUILDS WHEN MULTIPLE
/     FILES ARE OPEN SIMULTANEOUSLY, EACH NEEDING ITS OWN BUFFER.

/     EVEN WHEN BETTER OVERALL THROUGHPUT IS DESIRABLE, OS/8 STILL PROVIDES AN
/     INFERIOR SOLUTION: DUE TO THE OS/8 PROHIBITION ON THE USE OF THE LAST PAGE
/     OF EVERY MEMORY FIELD, THE MAXIMUM GENERALLY ALLOWED TRANSFER WOULD BE 15
/     RECORDS [30 PAGES].  ONLY EVEN VALUES FROM TWO THROUGH 30 CAN BE SPECIFIED
/     IN TERMS OF ALLOWABLE PAGE COUNT [DIVIDE BY TWO TO GET RECORD COUNT].  IN
/     ALL P?S/8 HANDLER CALLS, ANY VALUE IS ALLOWED IN THE RANGE OF ONE THROUGH
/     32.  P?S/8 HAS BOTH THE LARGEST MAXIMUM BUFFER SIZE AND THE SMALLEST
/     MINIMUM BUFFER SIZE AND ALL CASES IN-BETWEEN WHILE OS/8 CANNOT ALLOW ANY
/     ODD SIZES OR THE MAXIMUM SIZE OF 32. [NOTE: CERTAIN EXISTENT HARDWARE
/     DEVICES CANNOT RUN OS/8.  OS/8 DEMANDS A DESIGN QUIRK: THE DEVICE MUST BE
/     INHERENTLY PAGE-ORIENTED [AS IS IDEAL FOR ALL P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATIONS] OR,
/     IF THE DEVICE IS DOUBLE-PAGE RECORD-ORIENTED, THERE MUST BE A WAY TO
/     READ/WRITE THE FIRST 128 WORDS ONLY.  MOREOVER, THIS HAS TO BE
/     IMPLEMENTED WITHIN A DEVICE HANDLER THAT OCCUPIES AT MOST SOMEWHAT LESS
/     THAN TWO PAGES OF CODE SPACE.

/     SINCE P?S/8 ALLOWS JUST UNDER NINE PAGES OF CODE SPACE, THIS CAN GENERALLY
/     BE ACCOMPLISHED WITH EASE.  FOR EXAMPLE: P?S/8 ON THE RK8E/RK05 ADDRESSES
/     EACH 256-WORD RK05 RECORD TO THE NEAREST HALF SECTOR.  WHEN NECESSARY, AN
/     INTERNAL BUFFER WITHIN THE HANDLER IS USED TO IMPLEMENT FIXUPS FOR ALL
/     SPECIAL CASE CONSIDERATIONS SUCH AS WRITING ONLY ON THE SECOND HALF OF A
/     SECTOR; FOR ALL CASES ANALOGOUS TO WHAT OS/8 ALLOWS, THE BUFFERING SCHEME
/     IS NOT USED.

/     THE CESI MDC8 WITH 256 WORD RECORDS IS THE DESIGNATED STORAGE HARDWARE FOR
/     OMNI-8, A DEDICATED BOOTABLE APPLICATION SYSTEM THAT IS EXPLICITLY
/     DESIGNED TO MAXIMIZE PERFORMANCE ON THAT DEVICE, OFTEN WITH A NET STORAGE
/     SPACE OF 32 MWORDS PER HARD DISK.  OS/8 IS ONE OF THE *EMULATED* OPERATING
/     SYSTEMS SUPPORTED; HOWEVER, OS/8 CANNOT RUN ON THE MACHINE.  P?S/8 CAN RUN
/     ON THIS MACHINE IF 8K AVAILABLE; THE P?S/8 SHELL ENVIRONMENT CAN ADDRESS
/     THE ENTIRE MDC8 ENVIRONMENT OF TWO COMPLETE HARD DISKS WITH EASE.]
/     THE FULL CAPABILITY OF THE P?S/8 SYSTEM DATE WILL BE AVAILABLE TO THE
/     SHELL ENVIRONMENT.  ALL FILES WILL BE CAPABLE OF A UNIQUE DATE IN THE
/     RANGE OF 01-JAN-1900 THROUGH 31-DEC-2411.  THIS IS THE ONLY OPERATING
/     SYSTEM FOR A DEC-MADE PRODUCT WITH THAT WIDE A DATE RANGE.  AS SUCH, THERE
/     SHOULD NOT BE ANY FILE THAT REQUIRES ANY FORM OF DATE SPOOFING FROM THE
/     DAWN OF THE TWENTIETH CENTURY FORWARD.  THE LARGE STORAGE CAPABILITY WILL ALLOW
/     THE ENTIRE HISTORICAL RECORD OF THE PDP-8 TO BE STORED ON A SINGLE DEVICE THAT
/     CAN BE SHARED WITH ALL USERS FOR THE FORESEEABLE FUTURE.  THIS INCLUDES TEXT
/     FILES WRITTEN BY SEYMOUR CRAY IN 1960 DEFINING 12-BIT COMPUTING AND LATER
/     ARTICLES FROM MIT LINCOLN LABORATORIES IN SUPPORT OF THE LINC PROJECT WITH
/     ACCURATE ORIGINAL FILE DATES.  THE PDP-8 SHARES A HERITAGE OF DESIGN WITH THESE
/     OTHER TWO PREDECESSOR SYSTEMS; SUPPORTING DOCUMENTS SHOULD BE PART OF ANY PROPER
/     MASTER FILE STORAGE COLLECTION.

/     SHELL COMMANDS WILL BE TOTALLY IN LINE WITH DEC STANDARDS FOR OPERATING
/     SYSTEMS NEWER THAN OS/8.  FROM THE STANDPOINT OF AN OS/8 USER, THIS
/     ESSENTIALLY MEANS CCL-LIKE IMPLEMENTATION IN ALL SITUATIONS, WITHOUT THE
/     OVERHEAD OF OS/8'S IMPLEMENTATION OF CCL. [NOTE: OS/8 CCL IS SO
/     OVERHEAD-RIDDEN, DEC MANAGEMENT MADE OFFICIAL RECOMMENDATIONS NOT TO
/     ENABLE CCL ON SYSTEMS BASED ON SLOWER DEVICES SUCH AS DECTAPES AND
/     LINCTAPES.]

/     UNLIKE OS/8, PROGRAMS CAN DETERMINE THE EXACT MEANING OF DEFAULT DEVICES.
/     [NOTE: OS/8 ONLY SUPPORTS ONE DEFAULT DEVICE AT A TIME; THE SHELL ALLOWS
/     PROGRAMS TO SUPPLY UNIQUE POSITIONAL DEFAULT DEVICES WITHIN THE COMMAND.]
/     BY FORCING DEFAULTS TO BE DETERMINED FROM A SMALL SYSTEM CACHE OF UNIQUE
/     DEFAULT DEVICES, IT IS POSSIBLE TO OPEN MORE THAN ONE OUTPUT STREAM AT A
/     TIME.

/     FOR EXAMPLE, THE SHELL PDP-8 ASSEMBLER [TENTATIVELY TO BE NAMED XPAL] WILL
/     BE ABLE TO PERFORM ALL OPERATIONS IN TWO PASSES, NOT THREE AS IS DONE IN
/     OS/8. [NOTE: THE P?S/8 "PAL" ASSEMBLER NEARLY DOES THIS CURRENTLY, WITH
/     THE LONE EXCEPTION BEING THE LINEPRINTER OUTPUT MUST BE DIRECTED TO THE
/     PHYSICAL DEVICE 66 LINEPRINTER OR THE LOGICAL LINEPRINTER IF THE LOGICAL
/     CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED.]  THE ONLY REQUIREMENT IS THAT THE TWO OUTPUT
/     DEVICES ARE DIFFERENT FROM EACH OTHER.  WHILE THE USER CAN CREATE A
/     COMMAND ATTEMPTING TO VIOLATE THIS, THE SHELL WILL REJECT THIS AS
/     IMPOSSIBLE.  HOWEVER, BY DEFAULT, THE DEVICES WILL ALREADY BE UNIQUE.
/     THE ONLY CONFIGURATION THAT WOULD PREVENT SUCH OPERATION ENTIRELY WOULD BE
/     IF THE SYSTEM IS CONFIGURED TO ONLY EXIST AS BLOCKS ON THE SYSTEM DEVICE
/     WITH AN OFFSET AND THERE ARE NO OTHER LOGICAL DEVICES AVAILABLE.  IN THIS
/     CONTRIVED EXAMPLE, XPAL WOULD HAVE TO OPERATE IN A MANNER ANALOGOUS TO
/     OS/8 PAL8 USING TWO ASSEMBLY OPERATIONS: ONE TO PRODUCE BINARY AND ANOTHER
/     TO PRODUCE A LISTING FILE.  EXECUTABLE PROGRAMS CAN DEMAND AS MANY AS
/     THREE POSITIONAL DEFAULT DEVICES, ALL UNIQUE.  [NOTE: THIS IS SUBJECT TO
/     CHANGE; HOWEVER, IT IS HOPED THAT THIS SHOULD COVER ALL KNOWN CASES.]
/     XPAL WILL REJECT ATTEMPTS TO USE THE SECOND DEVICE IN A DEFAULT SITUATION
/     SHOULD THIS DEFAULT DEVICE NOT BE DEFINED.  FOR MOST CONFIGURATIONS, TWO
/     OR MORE DEVICE/LOGICAL UNITS WILL BE AVAILABLE TO ALLOW MAXIMUM
/     FUNCTIONALITY.  [CONTRAST THIS WITH OS/8 WHERE THIS FEATURE DOES NOT
/     EXIST; OS/8 DOES NOT ALLOW MULTIPLE OUTPUT FILES TO BE OPEN FOR PAL8 EVEN
/     IF LOCATED ON DIFFERENT DEVICES.  THUS, ONLY DEFICIENT CONFIGURATIONS WILL
/     BE REQUIRED TO OPERATE IN A LIKE MANNER TO OS/8 WITH REGARD TO ASSEMBLER
/     PASS CONSIDERATIONS.]

/     FOR RETRO-COMPATIBILITY ONLY, A COMMAND DECODE OPTION MAY BE MADE
/     AVAILABLE.  ALL SYSTEM PROGRAMS WILL BE DESIGNED TO NOT REQUIRE IT,
/     INSTEAD DEPENDING UPON THE SHELL TO PRE-PARSE THE ENTIRE COMMAND AND OPEN
/     ALL EXISTING AND TENTATIVE FILES.

/     GIVEN THIS LEVEL OF OPERATING SYSTEM SUPPORT, THE INTERNAL INTERFACE
/     PORTION OF MOST OS/8 PROGRAMS CAN EASILY BE REWRITTEN ALLOWING ALL USEFUL
/     APPLICATIONS TO BE MIGRATED TO THE P?S/8 SHELL.

/     THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE SHELL WILL TEND TO CHANGE CERTAIN SYSTEM
/     CONFIGURATIONS SUCH AS THE RK8E.  WHEN THE RK8E SYSTEM HANDLER WAS
/     ORIGINALLY DESIGNED, IT WAS NOT CONTEMPLATED THERE WOULD BE A NEED FOR
/     MORE LOGICAL BLOCKS PER DEVICE THAN THE BASIC P?S/8 UPPER LIMIT OF 4096
/     LOGICAL BLOCKS; BLOCKS BEYOND THIS RANGE CAN ONLY BE ADDRESSED IF THE
/     DEVICE MAPPING CONTINUES THE NEXT PHYSICAL BLOCK AS THE LOWEST BLOCK ON
/     THE NEXT LOGICAL UNIT.  THE P?S/8 SHELL CHANGES THE DESIGN AS THE
/     NON-SYSTEM HANDLERS HAVE A LARGER SCOPE OF BLOCK ADDRESSIBILITY.

/     AS SUCH, INSTEAD OF SUPPORTING LOGICAL UNITS 0 THROUGH 3 ON A SINGLE DISK
/     CARTRIDGE, LOGICAL UNIT 0 COULD ADDRESS AN ENTIRE RK05 PACK WHICH IS
/     BEYOND THE CAPABILITY OF OS/8 [WHICH REQUIRES TWO HANDLERS PER PACK].  BY
/     DEFINING THE SYSTEM CONFIGURATION TO INCLUDE TWO PHYSICAL PACKS, EACH
/     LOGICAL UNIT OF AN RK8E NON-SYSTEM HANDLER COULD ADDRESS AN ENTIRE RK05F
/     FIXED PACK OR A PAIR OF RK05/RK05J CARTRIDGE PACKS ARRANGED AS PHYSICAL
/     DRIVE 0 AND 1, 2 AND 3, ETC. [NOTE: A CONTROLLER MODIFICATION EXISTS KNOWN
/     AS THE RKS8E THAT ALLOWS UP TO 8 PACKS SIMILAR TO THE WAY RK05 PACKS ARE
/     DEFINED ON PDP-11 SYSTEMS.]

/     IN OS/8 TERMS, EACH RK05 PACK CONTAINS TWO DEVICES OF 3248 256-WORD
/     RECORDS WHERE THE MAXIMUM POSSIBLE IS 4096 RECORDS].  SINCE THE ENTIRE
/     PACK IS MORE THAN ONE OS/8 DEVICE, TWO DEVICES ARE REQUIRED.  BY
/     COMPARISON, THE ORIGINAL P?S/8 SYSTEM SUPPORTS FOUR LOGICAL UNITS PER PACK
/     EACH 3248 128-WORD SIZE BLOCKS.  THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT CAN UTILIZE AN
/     ENTIRE RK05 PACK THAT ADDRESSES 12992 128-WORD BLOCKS [25984 FOR RK05F
/     DEVICES OR A PAIR OF RK05J PACKS] WHERE THE P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE ADDRESSES
/     UP TO THE FIRST 4096 BLOCKS. [NOTE: THE SHELL DIRECTORY STRUCTURE PROVIDES
/     ENTRIES TO PROTECT THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM AREA; INTERNAL FILE ENTRIES WILL
/     BE AVAILABLE AS HIDDEN UNMOVABLE DIRECTORY ENTRIES FOR THIS PURPOSE, ETC.]
/     ASSUMING MODEST USAGE OF THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM AREA WITH ONLY A FEW TFS
/     FILES ALLOWED, ONLY THE FIRST 400 BLOCKS SHOULD BE REQUIRED FOR FULL
/     COMPATIBILITY WITH THE BASIC SYSTEM.  AS SUCH, OVER 12000 BLOCKS WOULD BE
/     AVAILABLE TO THE SHELL SYSTEM.  [COMPARE THIS WITH OS/8 REQUIRING TWO
/     DEVICE HANDLERS EACH ADDRESSING AROUND HALF OF THIS.  AND THIS SYSTEM
/     COULD BE CONFIGURED FOR LARGER DEVICE SIZE SUCH AS REQUIRING EITHER TWO OR
/     FOUR RK05 PACKS.]  BECAUSE OF THE SUPERIOR DIRECTORY DESIGN OF THE P?S/8
/     SHELL, THIS WOULD CREATE A FAR MORE POWERFUL ENVIRONMENT FOR ANY USAGE
/     RANGING FROM MANY SMALL FILES [WHERE OS/8 EASILY RUNS OUT OF DIRECTORY
/     SPACE] TO HANDLING FAR LARGER FILES THAN OS/8 CAN ADDRESS IN ANY
/     CONFIGURATION.  YET DESPITE THESE CONFIGURATIONAL DIFFERENCES, THE P?S/8
/     SHELL NON-SYSTEM DRIVERS CAN ADDRESS THE ENTIRE DISK USING SMALLER READ
/     AND WRITE BUFFERS [FOR A MINIMUM CONFIGURATION], OR LARGER READ AND WRITE
/     BUFFERS [DUE TO LIFTING RESTRICTIONS ON FILE BUFFERING THAT ONLY APPLY IN
/     OS/8 DUE TO VARIOUS LIMITATIONS.  OS/8 CAN ONLY ADDRESS FILES BY TWO-PAGE
/     BUFFERS OR MULTIPLES THEREOF UP TO A MAXIMUM SIZE OF 30.  P?S/8 PROGRAMS
/     CAN ALWAYS ADDRESS ANY FILE USING A SINGLE-PAGE BUFFER OR MULTIPLES
/     THEREOF UP TO A MAXIMUM OF 32.

/     AS SUCH, CHANGING THE SYSTEM CONFIGURATION ON THE RK8E WILL BETTER TAKE
/     ADVANTAGE OF THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT. [NOTE: THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM SUPPORTS
/     THE CONVRT PROGRAM TO TRANSFER TEXT FILES BETWEEN OS/8 AND P?S/8 IN BOTH
/     DIRECTIONS.  THIS PROGRAM REQUIRES THAT OS/8 DEVICES CAN BE ADDRESSED IN
/     THE SAME BOUNDARY CONDITIONS ON A DEFINABLE LOGICAL UNIT.  THE ORIGINAL
/     RK8E HANDLER WOULD THUS ALLOW CONVRT TO WORK ON LOGICAL UNITS 2, 4 AND 6
/     ASSUMING TWO CARTRIDGES.  IN THE NEW CONFIGURATION LOGICAL UNIT 1 WILL
/     WORK IDENTICALLY TO THE ORIGINAL SYSTEM USING UNIT 4.  THIS CONSIDERATION
/     WOULD BE CONSIDERED AN INTERIM STEP AS THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT CAN SUPPORT
/     AN INDEPENDENT UTILITY TO BE KNOWN AS PIPOS8 TO TRANSFER FILES BETWEEN THE
/     SHELL ENVIRONMENT AND AN OS/8 DEVICE MOUNTED ON A P?S/8 ADDRESSABLE
/     DEVICE.  THIS WILL ALLOW FILE TRANSFERS ON AN EQUAL BASIS IN BOTH
/     DIRECTIONS.] 

/ 22) TFS FILE SYSTEM

/     THE TINY FILE SYSTEM [TFS] IS THE PRIMARY FILE SYSTEM OF THE BASIC P?S/8
/     OPERATING SYSTEM.  IT IS A DIRECT DESCENDANT OF THE R-L MONITOR FILE
/     SYSTEM WITH WHICH IT IS PARTIALLY COMPATIBLE.

/     TFS FILES ARE FIXED SIZE INDEPENDENT FILES OF 2048 12-BIT WORDS.  ACTUAL
/     FILE CONTENTS IS CONTEXT-DEPENDENT; THERE ARE NO RULES OTHER THAN THE
/     FILE SIZE.  ENTRIES CAN BE MADE IN THE TFS DIRECTORY OVER OTHERWISE
/     UNDEFINED STORAGE SPACE IN ANTICIPATION OF FUTURE USE.  DEPENDING ON
/     SPECIFIC CIRCUMSTANCES, PERFORMANCE IMPROVEMENT CAN BE ACHIEVED BY CLEVER
/     FILE NAME PLACEMENT WITHIN THE DIRECTORY, ESPECIALLY ON SLOWER DEVICES
/     BASED ON DECTAPES OR LINCTAPES.

/     THE FILE STRUCTURE ONLY SUPPORTS AN UP TO SIX CHARACTER FILE NAME WITHOUT
/     EXTENSION; THERE IS NO DATE SUPPORT FOR TFS FILES.  THIS CAN BECOME EITHER
/     ITS STRONGEST POINT OR ITS WEAKEST POINT DEPENDING ON ACTUAL USAGE.  THE
/     TFS FIXED FILE CONCEPT IS NOT TO THE LIKING OF ALL USERS; HOWEVER, ONCE
/     ACCEPTED, IT GENERALLY PROVIDES GREATER PERFORMANCE UNLESS THE SIZE OF A
/     PROJECT OVERWHELMS THE TFS DIRECTORY CAPABILITY IN TERMS OF UNWIELDINESS.
/     FOR SMALL TO MEDIUM SOURCE CODE PROJECTS, EDITING A STRING OF TFS FILES
/     CAUSES FAR LESS OVERHEAD THAN MORE CONVENTIONAL FILE SYSTEMS [SUCH AS IS
/     USED IN THE OPTIONAL P?S/8 SHELL OR OS/8].  USERS EMBRACING THE TFS
/     DIRECTORY WILL QUICKLY DEVELOP A SENSE OF HOW TO ACCESS THE ACTIVE
/     PORTION OF A SOURCE CODE STREAM CONSISTING OF THE CONCATENATION OF SEVERAL
/     TFS FILES.  IT IS NOT NECESSARY TO MODIFY UNRELATED TFS FILES TO APPLY
/     EDITS TO ONE PORTION OF A PROGRAM; MERELY OPEN THE AFFECTED FILE, MAKE
/     CHANGES AND WRITE THE FILE BACK TO EXACTLY THE SAME EXACT FILE BLOCKS.  NO
/     BACKUP FILES ARE WRITTEN [UNLESS THE USER CREATES THEM EXPLICITLY] AND NO
/     OPERATIONS ARE PERFORMED TO UPDATE THE TFS DIRECTORY UNLESS ABSOLUTELY
/     NECESSARY. [NOTE: THE BASIC P?S/8 KEYBOARD EDITOR AND MONITOR OPERATES
/     WITH THE ENTIRE TFS DIRECTORY CACHED AT ALL TIMES.  BACKUP FILES CAN BE
/     CREATED AHEAD OF TIME AND FILE COPIES CREATED INSTANTLY WRITING ONLY TO
/     THE AFFECTED FILE BLOCKS ON THE CURRENT SYSTEM DEVICE LOGICAL UNIT; THE
/     TFS DIRECTORY WILL NEVER BE UPDATED NEEDLESSLY.]

/     A TYPICAL EXAMPLE OF CONVENTIONAL VARIABLE-LENGTH FILE EDITING VERSUS TFS
/     FILE EDITING FOLLOWS:

/     ASSUME A SINGLE FILE IN A CONVENTIONAL VARIABLE SIZE ENVIRONMENT IS 128
/     BLOCKS LONG AND IN A TFS ENVIRONMENT THE SAME SOURCE TEXT EXISTS IN EIGHT
/     TFS FILES TO BE USED AS A CONCATENATED STREAM WHEN ASSEMBLED.  EDITING IN
/     THE CONVENTIONAL ENVIRONMENT REQUIRES OPENING A FREE SPACE ON THE DEVICE
/     THAT IS AT LEAST 128 BLOCKS LONG; EACH SYSTEM MAY PROVIDE A WAY TO OBTAIN
/     A SUITABLE SECTION, OFTEN THE LARGEST CONTIGUOUS FREE SPACE CURRENTLY
/     AVAILABLE.  [NOTE: THE EDIT CANNOT EVEN BE PERFORMED IF SUCH SPACE IS NOT
/     PRESENTLY AVAILABLE; THE USER MAY BE FORCED TO PUT OFF THE EDIT AND DEAL
/     WITH COMPRESSING EMPTY SPACE TOGETHER BEFORE THE EDIT CAN BE PERFORMED.]
/     ONCE THE EDITING SESSION COMMENCES, THERE ARE NOW TWO AREAS THE SIZE OF
/     THE ENTIRE FILE IN PLAY SIMULTANEOUSLY.  CLOSING THE FILE LEADS TO THE
/     DECOMMITMENT OF THE ORIGINAL FILE BLOCKS; THIS IN TURN TENDS TO FRAGMENT
/     THE STORAGE DEVICE LEADING TO ADDITIONAL NEED TO COMPRESS OUT EMPTY SPACE
/     THE NEXT TIME, ETC.  THE NEW FILE ALSO TENDS TO LEAD TO FRAGMENTATION AS
/     THE FINAL FILE SIZE WILL TEND TO BE LESS THAN THE TEMPORARY ALLOCATION OF
/     STORAGE SPACE REQUESTED.  UNLESS THE STORAGE SYSTEM IS ONLY LIGHTLY USED,
/     DEFRAGMENTATION OF EMPTY SPACE WILL TEND TO BE NEEDED OFTEN.  [NOTE: THE
/     P?S/8 SHELL CANNOT HELP BUT SUFFER FROM THIS PROBLEM IN PRACTICAL USAGE;
/     HOWEVER, THERE ARE SOME WAYS TO MITIGATE THE PROBLEM SOMEWHAT AS COMPARED
/     TO OS/8'S RAW IMPLEMENTATION OF A VARIABLE SIZE FILE SYSTEM THAT WORKS
/     EXACTLY AS DESCRIBED IN THIS EXAMPLE.  THIS WILL INCLUDE SUCH AS FILE
/     LOCALIZATION TECHNIQUES AND THE ABILITY TO DEFINE TIERS OF SPACE
/     ALLOCATION; EDITING PROGRAMS CAN SPECIFY REQUESTING THE NEAREST EMPTY
/     SPACE ON THE DEVICE AS WELL AS ACCEPTABLE LIMITS ON THE ACTUAL SIZE OF THE
/     REQUESTED TENTATIVE FILE SPACE INSTEAD OF ALWAYS BEING PROVIDED THE
/     LARGEST AVAILABLE EMPTY SPACE ANYWHERE ON THE DEVICE.  SUCH TECHNIQUES
/     WILL TEND TO SOMEWHAT LIMIT FRAGMENTATION.] [NOTE: DETAILS OF THE OVERHEAD
/     OF CARRYING OUT THESE OPERATIONS HAS NOT BEEN EXAMINED; IT IS DEPENDENT ON
/     SPECIFIC IMPLEMENTATION; NO VARIABLE-LENGTH FILE SYSTEM ACCOMPLISHES THESE
/     OPERATIONS INSTANTANEOUSLY.]
/     ACCOMPLISHING THE EQUIVALENT EDIT IN THE TFS DIRECTORY INVOLVES MERELY
/     LOCATING THE ONE FILE WHERE THE EDITS MUST BE PERFORMED.  THE FILE IS
/     LOADED INTO THE EDITING BUFFER, EDITED IN PLACE AND WRITTEN BACK TO THE
/     SAME BLOCKS AS BEFORE THE EDIT. [NOTE: THE USER MAY OPTIONALLY LOAD THE
/     FILE, SAVE TO A PRE-ALLOCATED DESIGNATED BACKUP FILE, EDIT THE FILE AND
/     THEN WRITE IT BACK TO THE ORIGINAL STORAGE BLOCKS.]  BECAUSE THE TFS
/     DIRECTORY STRUCTURE IS 100 PERCENT CACHED, THERE IS *NO* OVERHEAD
/     ASSOCIATED WITH THE EDIT!

/     THE LARGER THE FILE, THE INHERENTLY MORE DRAMATIC THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN
/     THE TWO METHODS. [NOTE: THERE ARE TRADE-OFFS RELATED TO SUCH AS WHEN A
/     TFS FILE BECOMES TOO FULL INVOLVING SPLITING THE FILE INTO TWO FILES; THIS
/     MUST BE PERFORMED AS NEEDED.  AS LONG AS THERE IS ENOUGH ADDITIONAL SPACE
/     ON THE STORAGE DEVICE TO ALLOCATE ONE MORE TFS FILE, THIS CAN ALWAYS BE
/     ACHIEVED; CONTRAST THIS WITH THE NEED FOR ADDITIONALLY AT LEAST THE
/     STORAGE OF THE ENTIRETY OF THE CURRENT FILE SIZE IN A CONVENTIONAL
/     EDITING ENVIRONMENT. THE BASIC P?S/8 SYSTEM PROVIDES ADEQUATE UTILITIES TO
/     MANAGE EVERY ASPECT OF THIS PROCESS.]

/     ULTIMATELY, VERY LARGE PROJECTS CANNOT BE HANDLED BY THE TFS DIRECTORY
/     BECAUSE OF RESOURCE LIMITATIONS OF P?S/8. [NOTE: THERE ARE PROVISIONAL
/     WAYS AROUND MOST OF THE LIMITATIONS.] THERE IS A HARD UPPER LIMIT ON
/     PASSING TFS FILE HANDLES TO PROGRAMS OF 17 MAXIMUM, INCLUDING ANY REQUIRED
/     OUTPUT FILES.  FOR EXAMPLE, A PROGRAM MAY BE CREATED IN 14 TFS FILES THAT
/     CREATES THREE BINARY FILES.  DUE TO P?S/8 BATCH SUPPORT BEING PRESENT IN
/     THE OPERATING SYSTEM, THE USER CAN TYPE UP SHORT ["MAKE"-LIKE] COMMAND
/     FILES TO BE USED REPEATEDLY TO AVOID THE TEDIUM OF MANUALLY ENTERING LONG
/     COMMAND LINES.  FOR TRULY LARGE SOURCE CODE PROJECTS, A LARGER SYSTEM WILL
/     GENERALLY BE REQUIRED; THE P?S/8 SHELL WILL BE AN EXCELLENT WAY TO HANDLE
/     LARGER PROJECTS ASSUMING SUFFICIENT RESOURCES ARE AVAILABLE [SUCH AS MORE
/     MEMORY AND LARGER STORAGE DEVICES].

/ 23) .XOR.

/     MANY OPERATIONS WITHIN THE TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER ARE CARRIED OUT
/     BY A BIT-WISE EXCLUSIVE-OR OPERATION BETWEEN THE DECTAPE CONTROLLER STATUS
/     REGISTER "A" AND THE PDP-8 ACCUMULATOR [AC].  THE ".XOR." NOTATION IS USED
/     AS SHORT-HAND WHEN DESCRIBING THESE OPERATIONS.

/     A SUBTLE ISSUE COMPLICATES DESCRIBING THESE OPERATIONS: ONLY THE TEN
/     HIGHEST BITS ARE TRANSFERRED BY THE EXCLUSIVE-OR OPERATION; THE TWO LOWEST
/     BITS OF STATUS REGISTER "A" ARE USED TO PRESERVE CORRESPONDING CONTROLLER
/     FLAGS DIRECTLY IF SET.  ALL BITS OF THE AC ARE APPLIED TO STATUS REGISTER
/     "A" SIMULTANEOUSLY AS DESCRIBED ABOVE.

	$				/THAT'S ALL, FOLK!

